// (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_A2.md, row m12 = m4: KIRJ PROJ LUGE RÄÄK with the leads of modules 11–19; gates V1–V16 of
// docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B1.md §8). One storyline, one year before the B1 course (docs/COURSE_CAST.md): April. Sofia's friend Kati
// comes from Finland by ferry on Friday 16 April (12.30 Helsinki → 14.30 Tallinn). On Saturday 17 April they take the 9.15 train to
// Sofia's mother Helgi in Tartu (11.20); on Sunday 18 April the 16.00 Teekaaslane bus back is cancelled, the 18.00 bus arrives at
// 20.30, Kati only just catches the 21.30 ferry. Minor characters: bus driver Toivo (radio, host Ülle), cashier Urve, Dmitri (a trip
// to his aunt Nina in Valga, transfer in Tartu). The pictures of the Kasuta sheets (art/visuals/a2-module-12.js): 059 Anna's three
// pictures of her trip, 060 Markus and Anna at the town map.
//   056 KIRJ L→W  transport and the ticket: bussiga, jalgsi, peatuses / peatusesse / peatusest, üks ots, edasi-tagasi; corner W1 (a text
//                 from a business card); main: a 50–70-word letter to Kati on how to get there (W04), planned and edited.
//   057 PROJ L→S  the timetable and the trip plan: väljub Tallinnast, saabub Tartusse, hilineb kümme minutit, teiselt platvormilt;
//                 corner L1 (eight station announcements); main: the pair agrees on a plan (S03).
//   058 LUGE R→W  the ticket office and the rules: Mis kell …? Kust …? Kui palju …? Kas …?, kaks piletit; corner R1 (set phrases in
//                 short dialogues); main: a 60–80-word reply to the bus company (W08).
//   059 RÄÄK R→S  the simple past of a finished trip: käisin, läksin, tulin, nägin, sõitsin; corner S2 (one asks, the other answers,
//                 S05); main: the learner tells about a trip (S07); home recording: the picture (S06).
//   060 PROOV     mock 1, all four parts timed (B.examPart): W1, W2a, W2b, R1–R5, L1–L4, S0, S1, S2.
// Every teaching lesson: „Mäletad?” naming the previous lesson and one of modules 8–10, an in-lesson pair task, a home
// recording in Kasuta, two fluency tasks, one exam corner. No tingiv kõneviis (A2).
